# Project Context

This is a developer portfolio for the FlyRank Front-end AI Engineering capstone.

## Planned Technology Stack
- Next.js
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS

## Engineering Conventions
- Use TypeScript for application code.
- Prefer reusable React components.
- Build responsive, mobile-first interfaces.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible controls.
- Keep components small and maintainable.
- Avoid hardcoded secrets and credentials.
- Explain important implementation decisions.
- Do not claim unimplemented features are complete.

## AI Collaboration Rules
- Inspect existing code before making changes.
- Explain proposed changes clearly.
- Avoid modifying unrelated files.
- Ask before installing new dependencies.
- Recommend appropriate tests.
- Use Conventional Commits for Git history.

## Accessibility and Quality Checklist

Before considering a frontend task complete:

- Verify the layout at mobile, tablet, and desktop widths.
- Use semantic HTML elements.
- Ensure buttons and links are keyboard accessible.
- Give meaningful images descriptive alternative text.
- Avoid horizontal overflow on small screens.
- Explain any known limitations.
- Do not claim tests have passed unless they were actually run.

## Portfolio Evidence

This portfolio will demonstrate frontend engineering through
documented projects, working interfaces, and technical decisions.

Each completed project case study should include:

- The problem the project addresses.
- My personal contributions.
- Technologies actually used.
- A technical challenge and how I approached it.
- Screenshots or a working demonstration, where available.
- Known limitations and planned improvements.

